## 6. NocoDB EIP Table Schema

**Table ID:** `mhicpnrahaesxmy`

⚠️ **v4.0 CORRECTION:** v4.0 listed "Enriched Emotion Breakdown", "Enriched Pain Point Breakdown" (JSON arrays), and standalone "Core Emotion" column. These do not appear in the actual Step 14 write payload. Status unclear — see Gap #3.

**23 fields written by Step 14:**

| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| EIP Run ID | SingleLineText | EIP-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS-mmm |
| ALA Record ID | Number | FK → ALA table |
| EIP Timestamp | DateTime | ISO 8601 UTC |
| Enriched Emotion Tag | **SingleLineText** | Stores `core_emotion` — see Gap #4 |
| Enriched Pain Point | **SingleLineText** | `pain_point_sub_category` canonical name |
| Domain | **SingleLineText** | `pain_point_domain_confirmed` cluster label |
| Intensity Level | SingleSelect | Low / Moderate / High / Critical |
| Polarity Balance | Decimal | 0.00–1.00 |
| Dominant Pole | SingleSelect | Positive / Negative / Mixed |
| Certainty Score | Decimal | 0.00–1.00 |
| Ambiguity Flag | Checkbox | Boolean |
| Collapse flag | Checkbox | Always false currently (stub) |
| Masked Emotion Flag | Checkbox | Boolean |
| Cognitive Driver | SingleLineText | |
| Need State | SingleLineText | 6 controlled values |
| Signal Type | SingleSelect | 6 values — see Section 5 |
| Emotion Hypothesis | LongText | |
| Pain Hypothesis | LongText | |
| Keywords | SingleLineText | ALA pass-through, retained for SIA |
| Signal Weight | Number | Integer or null |
| Client ID | SingleLineText | |
| ESS Status | SingleSelect | Pending / Processing / Complete / Error |
| Error Log | LongText | null on clean write |

> **Field type change June 2026:** `Enriched Emotion Tag`, `Enriched Pain Point`, `Domain` changed from SingleSelect to SingleLineText to support multilingual canonical names. English values unchanged.

**Pass-through fields — NOT stored in EIP table:**
`lang` · `reviewer_handle` · `review_date` · `platform` · `star_rating` · `raw_text` · `ala_run_id`

---

## 7. Dictionary Injection Strategy

EIP injects ALL entries from the selected language pair on every record — no pre-filtering.

| Component | Tokens | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Dictionary content | ~14,750 | Eligible for OpenAI prompt caching (90% discount) |
| Review + context | ~600 | Unique per record — never cached |
| GPT output | ~250 | |
| **Total** | **~15,600** | |
| **Effective with caching** | **~2,075** | |
| **Cost per record** | **~$0.0072** | Confirmed viable at all client volume tiers |

Pre-filtering to ~10 entries was evaluated and rejected: requires a second GPT call, risks missing masked emotion entries, and saves fewer tokens than caching achieves without the quality risk.

---

## 8. Downstream Inheritance

| Agent | Receives | Method |
|---|---|---|
| ESS | All 23 EIP fields + 7 pass-throughs | Step 18a/18 ESS trigger payload |
| HSI | Same via ESS → HSI payload chain | Carried forward |
| SIA | Domain, Signal Type, Enriched Pain Point, Enriched Emotion Tag | Direct NocoDB read on scheduled trigger |
| BRA | Signal Type, Domain, Signal Weight | Via HSI → BRA payload |
| RDA | Inherited from BRA payload | No direct EIP access |

No downstream agent re-queries either dictionary. EIP pays the classification cost once.

---

## 9. Open Issues and Pending Fixes

**9.1 STEP 11 Semantic Collapse Detection — Non-Functional Stub**
Unconditionally sets `collapse_flag: false`, `collapse_warning: null`. No logic implemented. Field is written to NocoDB and forwarded to ESS but always false. Action: define spec and implement, or remove node and field.

**9.2 Dignity-Risk Signal — Language Mismatch**
Step 10 matches `emotion_category` against English strings. GPT outputs `emotion_category` in Spanish for `lang=es`. Spanish dignity/trust-risk records cannot receive Dignity-Risk Signal. Action: add Spanish keyword equivalents to the text-match list, or normalize `emotion_category` to English before Step 10.

**9.3 Step 9 — No Pain Domain Validation for Spanish**
English records validate `pain_point_domain_confirmed` against 13-item list. Spanish records have no presence or type check — a null domain would write to NocoDB silently. Action: add minimum presence + type check for Spanish at V1. Full domain list validation for V2.

**9.4 Step 18 — No onError Fallback on ESS Trigger**
ESS outage fails the entire EIP execution even though classification and NocoDB write already completed. Action: add `onError: continueRegularOutput` to Step 18.

**9.5 Step 8 — No Retry on GPT Call**
Transient OpenAI error fails the record. ALA's equivalent call has retry configured. Action: add retry-on-fail (3 attempts, 30s wait) to match ALA pattern.

**9.6 Step 17a — Dead Code**
`ala_patch_body` computed in Step 17a but Step 17 hardcodes its own body and never references it. Not a live bug but creates maintenance confusion. Action: either remove the computation from 17a or have Step 17 reference it.

**9.7 emotion_category — Computed but Never Persisted**
GPT produces `emotion_category`, carried through all nodes, dropped at Step 14. Not written to EIP table, not forwarded to ESS. Action: confirm if any downstream agent needs it. If yes, add to Step 14 and Step 18a. If no, remove from Step 9 and all pass-throughs.

**9.8 enriched_emotion_tag — Never Persisted**
Step 14 maps `core_emotion` (canonical dictionary name) to the "Enriched Emotion Tag" NocoDB column — not GPT's `enriched_emotion_tag` free-text label. The free-text label is never stored. Action: confirm design intent (see Gap #4).

**9.9 Step 3b — Lowercase lang Fallback Mismatch**
`record['lang']` (lowercase) does not match NocoDB ALA field `Lang` (capitalized). Fallback always returns undefined. Low-risk — primary source from Step 1 payload covers all real cases. Action: change `record['lang']` to `record['Lang']`.

